These are the splits used for Figure 2 as well as 8-11 in our paper which were generated as described in Section 4.

The filenames contain the following three parameters:
* d[0-1.0]: The target divergence given to the generation algorithm.
* s[0.05-.4]: The size of the training data used (as a fraction of the whole dataset).
* r: The random seed.

Regarding the MCD1-3 labels for CFQ, we have added them as separate files in this directory for clarity, but they
correspond to the following generated splits:
* mcd1.json = divergence_split_s0.4_d1_r4_0.json
* mcd2.json = divergence_split_s0.4_d1_r5.5_55.json
* mcd3.json = divergence_split_s0.4_d1_r4.5_0.json
